 The applicants described in this case are Mr John Beck, Mr Howard Copp, and Mr Kevin Bazeley. They are United Kingdom nationals who lodged applications against the United Kingdom under Article 34 of the Convention for the Protection of Human Rights and Fundamental Freedoms on 11, 12, and 11 January 1999, respectively. They were represented by Ms J. Gould, a solicitor practising in Birmingham, England. The case originated from these three applications (nos. 48535/99, 48536/99, and 48537/99).

